From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:44:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] A release's and a season's fortunes read the player's
 part, and a series' parts carry on through pilots, options and pickups

Brief 27's series, releases and market cluster (Parts 8, 12 and 13, loops 20 and 33 to 41). Each piece was built where
something later reads it, never as a word on its own.

The player's part now moves a film's run and a season's audience, weighted by the part's size and never deciding either:
a lead's exceptional work lifts an opening by about two fifths against a kind's range spanning ten times and more, and a
season's audience by a fifth of a natural log at most. A season reads only the judged days posted before the network's
next word, kept whole in the record, because the network's decisions are worked out again from the first season on every
asking; a save from before has none, so no word already given changes. Each run keeps its US weeks, the takings abroad
and their worldwide sum in one currency, with a critics' and an audience score the game simulates and says so.

Loop 33's "Different distributor" and "Limited release" and Part 12's "Territory-specific releases" were drawn from what
was the on-time share, so late, streaming and shelved come as they did. Each reaches the chart, the credit and the awards:
another distributor's later date is the premiere the Emmys and the Actor Awards read; a film abroad first is placed by
its run at home, or, where the two years differ, not at all, since the rules ask for both in one year and the game
doesn't decide which.

Pilots come from the slate each winter; the network's word in May reads the pilot's own quality and the player's part,
and a pickup becomes a series run by systems/series.ts with the player's character, its option taken up or let go as any
is. An open option now holds the next season's guaranteed episodes: an offer on those days says so, and the player
declines, gives the option up (the part that season goes to another actor, and the casting office stops offering parts
without an audition), or asks to be released, answered by a draw that reads how much the production wants them back. A
guest part played Strong or better is weighed for a recurring return before the next season; a recurring part may grow
at its option; a revived series may come back on another network of its kind, which renews it from its own chance.

9-1-1 and Abbott Elementary are continued after their verified baselines, every later season the simulation's and said
so, and the parts drawn from them are cast only in those seasons: until now a part "after its tenth" season of 9-1-1 was
posted for days in the real tenth. Slow Horses and Severance stay the catalog's: no part reads their seasons.

The save schema stays 94: every new field is optional and an older save reads as it did.

